    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### Feature Description\n\nMy system: `Linux KDE Neon (Ubuntu)`\n\n---\n\nHi\n\nI have 2 qTox profiles:\n1. A ClearNet profile for normal usage with family and friends.\n2. A Tor connected DeepWeb profile for anonymous usage. \n\n---\n\nWhen i need to run any of the 2 profiles, i have to either:\n1. Turn off the current profile (logout) and login to the other one.\n2. Or Run 2 qTox instances with each running a profile.\n\n- The problem with the first approach is that one of the profiles is always offline, i need them both online to receive messages on both.\n- The problem with the second approach is that i have 2 qTox KDE system tray icons at the bottom and it looks weird.\nIt looks weird and messy to have 2 qTox instances and windows running at the same time. \n\n---\n\nSo my suggestions are:\n1. To have all the profiles running in a single window, without the need for logout.\n2. To be able switch between the profiles easily, using for example a drop down menu when you click on the profile picture.\n3. To have all the profiles connected and running at the same time.\n4. To have a colored theme or a colored window frame to distinguish the profiles and not send messages through the wrong profile by mistake. Something like QubesOS window frames. Also a theme would suffice.\n\n---\n\nI believe this feature should be robust to emulate a [SimpleX](https://simplex.chat/) like behavior of multiple profiles.\nWhen you using a single profile and your ID is posted in several locations, it can be linked from clearnet and deepweb to de-anonymize you.\nIt's important to have all the profiles online and be able to switch between them easily, in a single window.\nSimpleX is high RAM usage and heavy on the system. It's much much better to have robust cheap C++ qTox running.\n\nThanks for reading my words.\n\n### Contribution\n\n- [ ] I would like to contribute to this feature",
